    "notes": "Live BTicino F461 (firmware 2.0.11 / WHO 13 device type 200 / WHO 1013 134.15.5.0) WHO 13 clock capture of 2026-10-26, 20:46-20:59 UTC, on the physical test plant (gateway clock UTC + 2 h), asked for in OpenWebNet-HA/OWNd#144 (comment 6426869553): does the F461 ACK, echo or store a clock write whose time-zone field is non-standard (0530, 124)? Sessions: one event-only listener for the whole run (00_listener.jsonl, 1500 s, stopped at 20:59:39 UTC) and one short probe invocation per step, each on its own command + event sessions (tools/probe.py, 3 s pause after each request); listener and probe both ran OpenWebNet-HA/OWNd#144 head da77a53 (the probe sends raw strings but refuses a frame its OWNd cannot parse, and OWNd master raises on a 0530 / 124 time zone). Steps: baseline reads *#13**0## / *#13**22## (999); *#13**#0*HH*MM*SS*0530##; *#13**#0*HH*MM*SS*124##; *#13**#22*HH*MM*SS*0530*W*DD*MM*YYYY##; the same with 124; each write followed by *#13**0## and *#13**22## read-backs; then the listener alone through the gateway's spontaneous 10-minute clock broadcast at 20:50:00 UTC (*#13**#1*01*26*10*2026## then *#13**#0*22*50*00*##, empty time-zone field); then the restore *#13**#0*HH*MM*SS*999## and its read-backs. Every request was ACKed in 9 - 18 ms (one read in 59 ms), every write with no reply, nothing was echoed on the event session within 3 s of any write nor anywhere in the listener window, every read-back reported 999, and the broadcast carried no 0530 / 124: the physical F461 neither stores nor echoes a non-standard time zone, and it did not echo the 999 restore either. The time field of each write (the shell's wall clock at expansion, 1 - 2 s before the send) was not in effect at its read-back: the read-backs kept following the wall clock (deduction at 1 s resolution). Every tx row carries both decodes of the written string: ownd_class / ownd_log from the #144 head (OWNGatewayCommand, timezone None, raw_timezone kept) and ownd_master_error from OWNd master (ValueError); every rx row carries ownd_class / ownd_log (what the #144-head listener logged at capture time, re-decoded offline to the same result) and ownd_master_class / ownd_master_log (identical: the F461 emitted only 999 and empty time-zone fields). Timing: t is the listener's clock, one monotonic axis over all runs, shifted so t = 0 is the baseline *#13**0## request; the probe's rows are placed on it through the frames both sessions received (capture.runs[].probe_segments[].listener_offset_s, spread <= 15 ms); tx.t = probe record time - 3 s pause - reply_time_s, result.t = tx.t + reply_time_s; command-session replies sit at the request's t (t_estimated); result.events_after holds the event-session frames of the pending window (tx.t <= t <= result.t), result.events_within_wait the frames the probe's own event session received between the send and the record 3 s later. A zone-2 temperature report (*#4*2*0*0240##) and a humidity report (*#4*2*60*39##) reached the listener during the broadcast wait and are kept as captured. A first attempt (frames with an empty time field, refused by the probe's OWNd before anything reached the gateway) is not included. Nothing is synthetic except the gateway's MAC and LAN address in the gateway block; the HMAC handshakes are not included.",
